# Build and run artifacts
build/
scratch/

# The disc image and anything extracted from it are the copyright holder's and are never committed.
#
# Kept NARROW on purpose. Everything extracted lands under scratch/ (already ignored above); the
# patterns here are the belt to that braces, for a file dropped in the repo root. Broad patterns
# (*.exe, *.bin) would also match ordinary prose naming those files in the docs.
*.chd
.env
# NOT listed here, deliberately: `SLUS_005.61` / `SLUS_*.*`. Every doc in this repo names them in
# prose, so a pattern that also swept prose would be unusable. The extracted executable lands under
# `scratch/bin/megamanx4/`, ignored above, which is where the tooling puts it; a copy dropped loose in
# the repo root is caught by review.

# The framework. Not tracked: either a relative symlink to the workspace's live psxport checkout
# (local) or a clone of its main (fresh machine). Managed by tools/psxport_fetch.py.
/external/psxport
# The vendored AGPL decomp is a REFERENCE; we never build it here, but a curious session might.
# external/mmx4/disks/ matters specifically: upstream's README says the retail SLUS_005.61 goes in
# disks/us, i.e. the natural way to use that repo is to drop OUR extracted executable into it.
external/mmx4/build/
external/mmx4/disks/
external/mmx4/.venv/
external/mmx4/expected/
*.log

# Python bytecode — never committed. Compiled .pyc embed ABSOLUTE SOURCE PATHS, i.e. a machine-path
# leak that a TEXT-only audit cannot see, because they are binary.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Editor / OS noise
compile_commands.json
.DS_Store
